<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fatima al-Fihri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 880</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatima">Fatima</a> al-Fihri was a woman from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a> who settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> in the Idrisid period with her family. Using her inheritance, she founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-al-qarawiyyin">al-Qarawiyyin mosque</a> in 859, which grew into one of the leading centres of Islamic learning. Her sister Maryam is credited with founding the Andalusian mosque of Fez.</p></div>
